The target function is `rapidcsv::Document::SetRow`. `SetRow` writes a row into the CSV at a given zero-based row index or by row label. It auto-expands missing rows, and if the input row is wider than current columns, it resizes data rows. Values are converted to strings before storing. Its signature is as follows:

```cpp
/**
     * @brief   Set row by index.
     * @param   pRowIdx               zero-based row index.
     * @param   pRow                  vector of row data.
     */
template<typename T>
    void SetRow(const size_t pRowIdx, const std::vector<T>& pRow);
/**
     * @brief   Set row by name.
     * @param   pRowName              row label name.
     * @param   pRow                  vector of row data.
     */
template<typename T>
    void SetRow(const std::string& pRowName, const std::vector<T>& pRow);
```

