1. `rapidcsv::Document::GetRowName`
    `GetRowName(pRowIdx)` returns the row label for a zero-based data row. Use it only when `LabelParams::pRowNameIdx >= 0` (e.g. set to 0 for first-column row headers). Otherwise it throws `out_of_range`. No direct example shown; docs mention `GetRowNames()`. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    /**
     * @brief   Get row name
